# Project structure (TanStack Start + Tailwind + Ant Design)

Stack: TanStack Start, file-based routing, Tailwind CSS, Ant Design UI. API: Laravel in `backend/` (see **`backend-module-structure.mdc`**).

## Backend (`backend/`)

Laravel API uses **[nwidart/laravel-modules](https://nwidart.com/laravel-modules/v6/introduction)** under `Modules/{Name}/` (controllers, requests, models, services, module routes). `routes/api.php` is shell-only; full layout: **`backend-module-structure.mdc`**.

## Top-level `src/`

| Folder | Role |
|--------|------|
| `routes/` | App shell only: `__root.tsx`, global layouts |
| `core/` | Platform infrastructure shared by all modules (not app UI) |
| `modules/` | Feature modules; `app` is the shell / shared app module |

Import alias: `@/…` → `src/…` (e.g. `@/core/api/client`, `@/modules/app/pages/HomePage`).

## `core/` — platform only

Folders: `api`, `configs`, `requestHandler`, `styles`, `i18n`, and other cross-cutting infra.

- `core/styles/` — global CSS
- `core/configs/` — env, app config
- `core/api/`, `core/requestHandler/` — axios client, interceptors
- `core/i18n/` — paraglide output, `localeLabels.ts`; locales: `en`, `ar`, `fa`, `tr`, `ru`, `zh` (base: `en`; RTL: `ar`, `fa`)

Do **not** put app shell components, providers, hooks, or page-level types in `core/`.

## `modules/app/` — shared application layer

The `app` module holds everything for the main app shell and routes used at `/`:

`components`, `providers`, `constants`, `hooks`, `types`, `utils`, `pages`, `routes`, `layouts`, `api`.

- **`components/`**, **`providers/`**: `Ct*` naming; group shell UI under `components/layout/`, loaders/errors under `feedback/`, i18n under `locale/`, composites under `widgets/` (e.g. `widgets/table/`)
- **`pages/`**: `*Page.tsx` (e.g. `HomePage.tsx`)
- **`routes/`**: file routes for app pages (`index.tsx`, `about.tsx`, …)
- Import from `@/modules/app/…` in `src/routes/__root.tsx` and router setup

## Other `modules/{name}/` — feature modules

Follow **`module-patterns.mdc`** — `modules/book/` is the reference implementation (services → hooks → routes → pages). Scaffold with `bun run create:module <name>`.

- Register routes in `src/routeTree.config.ts` as children of `_panel` via `layout('_panel', …)` (see below)
- Do not duplicate shell components; reuse `@/modules/app/components/…` when needed

## File-based routing & layouts

1. **Root shell**: `src/routes/__root.tsx` — HTML document, providers, footer (no page chrome)
2. **Panel layout** (app module only): `src/modules/app/layouts/_panel.tsx` + `CtPanelLayout` — full-width `CtHeader`, `<Outlet />` for child routes
3. **App pages**: `src/modules/app/routes/*.tsx` — flat route files (e.g. `index.tsx` → `/`, `about.tsx` → `/about`), mounted under `_panel` in `routeTree.config.ts`
4. **Features**: `src/modules/{feature}/routes/` — mount inside `layout('_panel', …)` with a URL prefix, e.g. `physical('/grades', '../modules/grades/routes')`

`routeTree.config.ts` wraps app and feature routes under `_panel`. Only the app module defines layouts; feature modules do not add their own panel layout.

## When adding code

| What | Where |
|------|--------|
| Axios client, env, i18n runtime, global CSS | `core/` |
| Header, footer, app providers, home/about pages | `modules/app/` |
| Feature UI, API, routes | `modules/{feature}/` |
| Laravel feature API (HTTP, models, services) | `backend/Modules/{Name}/` |

- SPA: `src/start.ts` → `defaultSsr: false`; `vite.config.ts` → `spa: { enabled: true }`. No per-route `ssr: false` unless opting back into SSR.
- Forms: react-hook-form (see `forms.mdc`)

## Do not

- Put shell components or app providers in `core/`
- Put feature logic in `src/routes/` (except `__root`)
- Nest API calls as `gradeApi.createGrade()` — use named exports (`getGrades`, `createGrade`)
- Skip `.gitkeep` in empty scaffold folders
